    "created_at": "2017-06-05T11:54:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-05T11:54:17Z",
    "body": "I think this change is slightly wrong... the list is of concepts that selectors match against, rather than a list of kinds of selectors. \"ID\" and \"class\" are DOM concepts, and CSS has selectors to match against those.\r\n\r\nWith that understanding in mind, the current text is not ambiguous I believe. But certainly it could be made clearer. Maybe adding an example is better?",
