    "updated_at": "2017-06-05T12:28:43Z",
    "body": "I can see the reasoning, but the line currently suggests that IDs and classes always are case-insensitive in quirks mode. Since IDs and classes in quirks mode match differently depending on which type of selector they are used in (where `.foo` does not always yield the same result as `[class=\"foo\"]`), it does not seem correct to make a general statement about them. This was a source of confusion in an implementation: https://github.com/tmpvar/jsdom/issues/1877#issuecomment-305941162\r\n\r\nI could potentially remove the list item and add a new paragraph above instead, describing the special case with IDs and classes along with an example.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
