    "created_at": "2017-06-05T13:40:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-05T13:40:30Z",
    "body": "In the years this Quirks Mode exception was spread in various documents, an example:\r\n\r\n> In quirks mode CSS class and id names are case insensitive. In standards mode they are case sensitive.  (This also applies to getElementsByClassName.)\r\n\r\ntaken from: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Mozilla_quirks_mode_behavior\r\n\r\nThat rule is not targeting an api method, it just generically states that those CSS identifiers should be handled using a case insensitive comparison.\r\n\r\nTo me, not an English expert (and not my native language), it simply means that the behavior of getElementsByClassName should be the same of other similar API querying the document for class names while in Quirks Mode.\r\n\r\nI will obviously accept any resolution here, my attempt is just to find uniformity in the implementations (if possible). This probably requires disambiguating some wording which is currently confusing and at time contradictory.\r\n",
